 Member 2 (Clinical Pathways Specialist): Coordinates recommendations from the IAT and DET, ensuring a comprehensive approach considering all diagnostic elements and management strategies.
 Member 3 (Clinical Pharmacologist): Evaluates the need for antibiotic therapy and other necessary medications, optimizing pharmacological interventions while considering the patient’s hepatic function and other comorbidities.


